   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [50d].** F site, all four j: 8.9·10⁻⁴⁷. A site, all four triples: 3.5·10⁻⁴². RV product formula (σ = 123, 432, 241, 314), all 256 words × 256 states: 5.3·10⁻⁴². Polynomial-gauge form with N_x: 5.2·10⁻⁴².\n\n**The dictionary (verified).** With Q_i(u) = z_i^{u/h}Φ(u)q_i(u), Φ(u) = V₄(u)Φ(u−h):\n\n⟨a₁,k₂,a₃,k₄|Ψ⟩ = ⟨0|Ψ⟩ · [Q(θ₂)/Q(θ₂−h)]^{k₂} [Q(θ₄)/Q(θ₄−h)]^{k₄} · D_{a₁}(θ₁)/D₀(θ₁) · D_{a₃}(θ₃)/D₀(θ₃),\n\nQ = any single-index Q_j; D_a(θ) = det_{i∈I, j∈{1,2,3,4}∖{a+1}} Q_i(θ − jh) for any triple I (columns at θ−h, θ−2h, θ−3h, θ−4h with the (a+1)-th omitted). **In this gauge N_x = 1: the existing words already are the RV-normalised basis, ⟨x̃| = ⟨x|.** In terms of the polynomials q̂_i(u) = z_i^{u/h}q_i(u): ⟨x|Ψ⟩/⟨0|Ψ⟩ = N_x ∏_F[q̂_j(θ_F)/q̂_j(θ_F−h)]^{k} ∏_A det[q̂_i(θ_A−jh)]_{j∈S_a}/det[q̂_i(θ_A−jh)]_{j=2,3,4}, with\n\nN_x = ∏_F V₄(θ_F)^{k_F} · ∏_A ∏_{b=1}^{a_A} V₄(θ_A − bh), V₄(u) = ∏_A(u−θ_A)∏_F(u−θ_F−h);\n\nat the standard point V₄(θ₂) = −2263/14000 (= k₁ of notes §12), V₄(θ₄) = 175491/78848; site 1: −1073/30184, 46092861/9110738560, 30636864570897/5499970653900800 (a = 1, 2, 3); site 3: 7857/745360, −340215957/555561529600, 55399745790009/828186683405312000.\n\n**Which Q on which site.** F sites (t₁ powers): a single-index Q, and *any* of Q₁..Q₄ gives the same ratio (two-term Baxter relation at u = θ_F). A sites (t_a at θ_A−h): a 3×3 Casoratian of three single-index Q's (= a single upper Q^l up to Hodge duality), any triple. In the nesting adapted to ⟨0| (4 → 34 → 234; the project's 'Q₁' = Q₄, 'Q₁₂₃' = Q₂₃₄ for highest-weight states): F ↔ 'Q₁', A ↔ 'Q₁₂₃' = W('Q₁','Q₂','Q₃') — **Paul's expectation is right.** The alternative reading of the task (the dual Q governs F because only the z₄V₄ term of τ₁ survives at θ_F) mixes up the nesting: the z₄V₄ term carries the *first-level* Q (Q₄), because the reference vacuum is killed by the upper-triangular T_ij; and at θ_F all four Q_j give the same ratio anyway. Shifts: the F site needs no shifted products — powers of t₁ at the single point θ_F (ratio Q(θ_F)/Q(θ_F−h)); products ∏t₁(θ_F+jh) would not telescope (at θ_F + h three terms of τ₁ survive).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. RV B-operator: the separated variables of the words\n\nB(u) = Σ_{k₁≤3}Σ_{|K₂|=2} T_{k₁1}(u) qmin_{K₂;(1,k₁+1)}(u+h) qmin_{123;(1,K₂+1)}(u+2h) (untwisted T, `sov-companion-L4.wb`). Exact test of the eigenvalue ratios β_w(u)/β₀(u) = ∏_A (u−θ_A)/(u−θ_A+a h) · ∏_F ((u−θ_F−h)/(u−θ_F))^k.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "sqTun[v_] := sqTun[v] = sqMono[sqLax1, v, 4];\nsqQminU[rows_, cols_, v_] := Sum[Signature[p] (Dot @@ Table[sqTun[v - (k - 1) sqH][[rows[[p[[k]]]], cols[[k]]]], {k, Length[cols]}]), {p, Permutations[Range[Length[rows]]]}];\nsqBop[v_] := sqBop[v] = Sum[sqTun[v][[k1, 1]] . sqQminU[K2, {1, k1 + 1}, v + sqH] . sqQminU[{1, 2, 3}, Join[{1}, K2 + 1], v + 2 sqH], {k1, 1, 3}, {K2, Subsets[{1, 2, 3}, {2}]}];\nsqBeig[w_, v_] := Module[{b = sqW[[sqWordIndex[w]]], bb, p, lam}, bb = Normal[b . sqBop[v]]; p = Ordering[Abs[b], -1][[1]]; lam = bb[[p]]/b[[p]]; {lam, bb == lam b}];\nsqBpred[w_, v_] := Product[If[sqTypes[[s]] == \"A\", (v - sqTh[[s]])/(v - sqTh[[s]] + w[[s]] sqH), ((v - sqTh[[s]] - sqH)/(v - sqTh[[s]]))^w[[s]]], {s, 4}];\nsqBwords = {{1, 0, 0, 0}, {2, 0, 0, 0}, {3, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0, 0}, {0, 2, 0, 0}, {0, 3, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 2, 0}, {0, 0, 3, 0}, {0, 0, 0, 1}, {0, 0, 0, 2}, {0, 0, 0, 3}, {2, 1, 3, 2}};\nsqB0 = sqBeig[{0, 0, 0, 0}, 37/100];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[With[{e = sqBeig[w, 37/100]}, {w, e[[2]], e[[1]]/sqB0[[1]] == sqBpred[w, 37/100]}], {w, sqBwords}],\n  {\"word\", \"B-eigenbra (exact)\", \"β_w/β₀ = prediction (exact, u = 37/100)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
