  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [50d].** Completeness with the exact measure: |Σ⟨Ψᴸ|y⟩M_{yx}⟨x|Ψ⟩/⟨Ψᴸ|Ψ⟩ − 1| ≤ 1.7·10⁻⁴³ (16 states). The Q-only formula Σ τ̃_y M_{yx} τ_x reproduces 1/𝒩 = ⟨Ψᴸ|Ψ⟩/(⟨0|Ψ⟩⟨Ψᴸ|0̄⟩) to all printed digits, e.g. 1/𝒩 = 1.34769411783622·10⁻⁴ for both extremal states (vacuum, weight (2,0,0,−2), and weight (−2,0,0,2)), 3.58531149696525·10⁻⁴ and 6.6468836011383·10⁻⁶ for two other states (python ordering differs from the Mathematica block ordering, so compare by weight). Note 1/𝒩 also depends on the normalisation of the ket vacuum |0̄⟩ and on the dual-side constants N_A, N_{F,n} (§9).\n\n**Determinant form (open).** A GLMR-type ansatz 1/𝒩 ∝ det_{12×12}⟨⟨…⟩⟩ — rows (a, site), columns (b, β), two-point brackets per site (bra points θ_F−h, θ_F with ket functions shifted by 0, h, 2h; mirror on A sites), u^{β−1}, free site weights, 4 shift orientations — was probed by a linearised fit with random separable test functions (300 samples, 256 monomial unknowns): residuals 6·10⁻⁵–1.3·10⁻³ (not exact) and the product form of the weights is violated. So the simplest GLMR transplant does not hold; a determinant form of the mixed 4/4̄ measure remains open.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
