   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12; python-verified, Wolfram cells not yet run)\n\n1. **Setup** [exact]: t₁, t₂, t₃ (companion and diagonal twist), calibrations (i)–(iii) reproduced (note: (i) needs a BPS reference v⊗w⊗v⊗w, v·w = 0; it fails for a generic product); word basis rank 256.\n2. **Spectrum** [50d]: 256 joint eigenstates (55 weight blocks of t^Λ, |Ψ_c⟩ = R|Ψ_d⟩), simple joint spectrum; **⟨0|Ψ⟩ ≠ 0 for all 256** (vacuum cyclic).\n3. **Q's** [50d]: Baxter Σ(−1)^aτ_a(u)Q(u−ah) = 0; Q_i = z_i^{u/h}Φq_i, Φ(u) = V₄(u)Φ(u−h); deg q_I = 2 + Σ_{i∈I}μ_i (|I| ≤ 3); Casoratians = vacuum factors F₂, F₃, F₄ × q_I (remainders 10⁻⁴³); q₁₂₃₄ state-independent; vacuum nesting 4 → 34 → 234.\n4. **Dictionary** [50d, 256 words × 256 states]: ⟨a₁,k₂,a₃,k₄|Ψ⟩ = ⟨0|Ψ⟩ ∏_{F}[Q(θ_F)/Q(θ_F−h)]^{k} ∏_{A} D_a(θ_A)/D₀(θ_A), F: any single-index Q; A: D_a = det_{i∈I, j∈{1..4}∖{a+1}} Q_i(θ_A − jh), any triple (Casoratian W(Q_i,Q_j,Q_k) for a = 0, 3; gapped for a = 1, 2); **N_x = 1 in the Γ-gauge** (polynomial gauge: N_x = ∏_F V₄(θ_F)^k ∏_A∏_{b≤a}V₄(θ_A−bh)). Equivalent to RV2 (5.20) with x = B-zeros (F: {θ_F, θ_F+h}, A: {θ_A..θ_A−3h}∖{θ_A−ah}) and Q^RV(u) = Q(u−h), any σ. Paul's expectation (single-index Q on the t₁-built F sites, W(Q₁,Q₂,Q₃) on the t_a-built A sites) confirmed; powers at one point, not shifted products, on F sites.\n5. **Dual basis / measure** [exact]: ket SoV basis on |0̄⟩ = e₄⊗e₁⊗e₄⊗e₁ (A: t₁(θ_A)^m; F: t_n(θ_F+nh)) has mirror-image dual wave functions (A: single dual Q; F: Slater of three dual Q's) [50d]; Gram matrix charge-graded (S_x + S_y = 12), triangular, 1456 nonzeros — **no diagonal measure**; the exact triangular measure M = G⁻¹ gives ⟨Ψᴸ|Ψ⟩/(⟨0|Ψ⟩⟨Ψᴸ|0̄⟩) = Σ τ̃_y M_{yx} τ_x entirely from Q-values (checked); 48 of the 256 dual vectors are single ket words.\n6. **Open:** determinant (GLMR-type) form of the mixed measure / of 1/𝒩 (simplest ansatz fails); identification of the ket basis as eigenbasis of a C-operator; ABJM point θ_A − θ_F = 2h (B degenerate, outside RV genericity).\n\nPython module and data: `sov_l4.py` (sections 1–8 + `main()`), session scratchpad `sovq/`.",
